 "human_notes": {
  "order": [
   {
    "note": "A knife comes first and is the only real prerequisite in the mod - it gates the cutting board and is worth carrying before any cooking exists. Guides reach for flint before iron.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:flint_knife",
     "farmersdelight:iron_knife"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Cutting board second. It is planks + a stick, so it is not a resource gate, it is a knowledge gate - it does nothing until a knife is in hand.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:cutting_board"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Cooking pot third, once any heat source exists. This is where the mod stops being a tool mod and starts being a food mod.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:cooking_pot"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Stove fourth - guides treat it as the upgrade that makes cooking permanent rather than a new capability.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:stove"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Skillet last of the core four, and framed as cheap (one brick, four iron) and dual-purpose.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:skillet"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "ladder": [
   {
    "note": "Knife tier ladder, purely a durability/speed climb - the flint knife already unlocks every cutting-board recipe, so later tiers are convenience, not access.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:flint_knife",
     "farmersdelight:iron_knife",
     "farmersdelight:golden_knife",
     "farmersdelight:diamond_knife",
     "farmersdelight:netherite_knife"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Heat ladder: a campfire under the pot works, but the stove is the real rung - one guide stresses it is a 'constantly lit oven' that cooks 'without wasting fuel', so it replaces the campfire rather than supplementing it.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:cooking_pot",
     "farmersdelight:stove",
     "farmersdelight:skillet"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Soil ladder for the farming half: organic compost converts dirt into rich soil, which is the mod's growth-rate upgrade over plain farmland.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:organic_compost",
     "farmersdelight:rich_soil",
     "farmersdelight:rich_soil_farmland"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "gates": [
   {
    "note": "The cutting board is inert without a knife held in hand. Stated explicitly: 'you also need the knife to use this cutting board'. An axe also works for some cuts, giving different results.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:cutting_board",
     "farmersdelight:flint_knife"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "The cooking pot must sit ON a heat source - it does not burn its own fuel. Campfire, stove and even lava all work; a guide is visibly surprised that lava does.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:cooking_pot",
     "farmersdelight:stove"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Skillet cooking needs heat underneath too - 'You need to put a stove underneath, okay? It's mandatory.' As a weapon it needs nothing.",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:skillet",
     "farmersdelight:stove"
    ]
   },
   {
    "note": "Every crop is gated behind finding its wild plant in the right biome first: cabbage on coastal shores, onion in plains/forest, tomato in plains, rice in wet areas (jungle and swamp).",
    "ids": [
     "farmersdelight:wild_cabbages",
     "farmersdelight:wild_onions",
     "farmersdelight:wild_tomatoes",
     "farmersdelight:wild_rice"
    ]
